Program Bug_2_12_DonotprefixDesync;
// Bug 2.12: `@donotprefix <symbol>` never compiles, in any configuration.
// Parser::PreprocessSingle's "donotprefix" handler reads
// m_currentToken.m_value (the symbol-name argument) and appends it to
// m_doNotPrefixSymbols, but never calls Eat() to actually consume that
// argument token - same dropped-token desync shape as 2.8. Compare to
// the sibling `@donotprefixunit` (no argument), which works fine, and to
// `@donotremove`'s handler a few lines above, which does call Eat() on
// its own symbol-name argument.
//
// Method B (compile-time desync), no VICE step. Confirmed live: placed as
// a plain top-level directive (the shape tried here), this fails with
// "After declarations, BEGIN is expected" - the dropped symbol-name token
// shifts everything after it, so the parser never finds a valid `var`/
// `begin`. Pre-fix expected behavior: compile failure with that error.
// There is no known-good variant to fall back on (unlike 2.8/2.9): every
// configuration tested for this directive fails the same way. Post-fix,
// this should compile clean.

@donotprefix myVar

var
	myVar : byte;

begin
	myVar := 5;
	loop();
end.
